-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  coff_pdb_link.adam - A debug build's PDB from Adam's linker (M7d): this
  program is the sample. Built debug, its exe names its PDB in a CodeView
  debug directory entry and the PDB is written beside it; it reads both
  back: the entry (type, age, the PDB's file name alone), the GUID and age
  the same in the exe and the PDB, every hash table of the PDB checked
  (PdbText: no name missing, no type hash that differs, every GSI bucket in
  order), no absolute path among its file names, then its own module (its
  symbol stream decoded: routines, parameters and locals with their types
  by Adam name, globals; its source lines), the linker's module and its
  globals and UDTs by name. Compiler units it imports (Adam.Pdb.*) bring
  their own CodeView, so the merge runs over many objects.
*******************************************************************************/

/*
@@test
  kind run
  exitcode 0
  | area 12 count 1
  | program path plain true
  | debug directory size 28 type 2
  |   record 0x53445352 age 1 name 'coff_pdb_link.pdb' size 42
  | identity same true signature from guid true
  | name name # '$P:res/tests/coff/coff_pdb_link.adam' found
  | module 'coff_pdb_link.exe' symbols true
  | module 'coff_pdb_link' files 1
  |   objname ''
